  "problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\pi $ belong?\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$\n- $R$\n- $Q$\n- $C$",
  "worked_solution": "The number $-\\pi $ is not a rational number. Consequently, $-\\pi $ does not belong to any of the sets  ${Q}^{-}$ nor $Q.$\n\nHowever, $-\\pi $ is a real number, so it belongs to $R.$\n\nFinally, since every real number is also a complex number, $-\\pi $ also belongs to $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"",
